        # 2
        {"kind": "h1", "text": "2. Overview & Summary"},
        {"kind": "h2", "text": "2.1 Problem Statement"},
        {"kind": "para", "text": "Search Console data is the only first-party record of how HaorGrix properties and client sites actually perform in Google Search, but reaching it means either the web UI (manual, unexportable at scale, capped rows) or bespoke scripts against the API. Agent-driven SEO work — CTR triage, position-change analysis, indexation checks, sitemap submission — stalls because the agent cannot read or act on that data itself. The evidence of the gap is already in the repository: six loose one-off TypeScript scripts sit in the project root, each written to answer a single question once."},
        {"kind": "h2", "text": "2.2 Proposed Solution"},
        {"kind": "para", "text": "A Node/TypeScript MCP server that exposes the Search Console and Indexing APIs as 10 tools over stdio: seven read tools and three write tools. Authentication is a Google service account supplied through GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS; the default property comes from GSC_SITE_URL. Two of the read tools are derived rather than pass-through — get_ctr_rescue_candidates and get_position_changes compute an answer the API does not return directly, which is where most of the server's value sits."},
        {"kind": "h2", "text": "2.3 Background & Context"},
        {"kind": "para", "text": "The server was built in July 2026 alongside the SEO Growth Engine workstream and is registered locally in the Claude configuration together with the GA4 MCP server. It is version 1.0.0 and functional, but it carries the marks of fast delivery: no test suite, no README, hand-written JSON schemas instead of zod, and the oldest MCP SDK pin in the monorepo."},
        {"kind": "h2", "text": "2.4 Strategic Fit"},
        {"kind": "para", "text": "Search Console is the entry point of the SEO data chain — impressions and positions here explain the sessions GA4 reports and the pages the WordPress MCP server edits. Making it agent-readable is what lets an agent close the loop from diagnosis to fix without a human copying numbers between tabs."},
        {"kind": "h2", "text": "2.5 Objectives & Business Value"},
